#: ../../adr/0011-extended-scene-imaging.md:1
msgid "ADR-0011: Scenes and the imaging of extended scenes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0011-extended-scene-imaging.md:3
msgid "**Status**: accepted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0011-extended-scene-imaging.md:4
msgid "**Date**: 2026-10-17"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0011-extended-scene-imaging.md:5
msgid "**Plan step**: P8.1 and P8.5 (REQ-SCN-1, REQ-SCN-6)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0011-extended-scene-imaging.md:7
msgid "Context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0011-extended-scene-imaging.md:9
msgid ""
"Scenes mix point sources and diffuse objects in a frame (celestial, "
"terrestrial, laboratory). Diffuse objects are incoherent: their image is "
"the sum of the images of their points. REQ-SCN-6 asks for three imaging "
"strategies (convolution, field-dependent PSFs, explicit decomposition), "
"chosen automatically, forcible, and logged; the convolution must be "
"refused for systems that are not shift-invariant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0011-extended-scene-imaging.md:14
msgid "Decision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0011-extended-scene-imaging.md:16
msgid ""
"**Scenes.** A `Scene` is a registered group type (`.lumos` group entries "
"carry `\"group_type\"`) whose child `combiner` holds the frame, the "
"pointing or site, the distance (laboratory) and the angular grid of the "
"scene. Components are connected by the type of their output: `SourceList`"
" to the `sources` output, `RadianceField` to the `radiance` output, "
"resampled onto the scene grid with flux conservation. Laboratory maps "
"keep their radiance and get angular pixels `dx / d` (radiance "
"invariance); the curvature of close objects is neglected, explicit fields"
" (lasers, lamps) cover that case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0011-extended-scene-imaging.md:23
msgid ""
"**Imaging.** Instruments stay models of objects at infinity: the entrance"
" of an imaging system is an input accepting a `SourceList`. "
"`image_scene(scene, ImagingSystem(ctx, entrance=..., exit=...), "
"strategy=...)`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0011-extended-scene-imaging.md:26
msgid ""
"`\"decomposition\"`: every pixel becomes a point source of flux `L ΔΩ`; "
"all are computed at once as modes of an `IncoherentBundle` (batches of "
"1024). The element `SceneToSources` does the same inside a graph."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0011-extended-scene-imaging.md:28
msgid ""
"`\"isoplanatic\"`: the on-axis PSF per unit flux density is computed by "
"the system; the plate scale is measured from the windowed centroids of "
"two off-axis PSFs; the scene is resampled onto an odd-sized angular grid "
"whose pixels map onto the detector pixels and convolved with FFTs "
"(`scipy.signal.fftconvolve`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0011-extended-scene-imaging.md:31
msgid ""
"`\"anisoplanatic\"`: PSFs at a grid of field points (snapped to whole "
"detector pixels), recentred, combined with bilinear weights (weighted "
"convolutions)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0011-extended-scene-imaging.md:33
#, python-format
msgid ""
"`\"auto\"`: probe a point at a quarter of the field: same total power "
"within 1 % and, shifted back by whole pixels, the same PSF within 1 % in "
"L1 norm over the common pixels → isoplanatic; otherwise decomposition. "
"Forcing `\"isoplanatic\"` on a system failing the probe raises an error. "
"The choice and its reason are logged on `lumos.scenes` and returned in "
"`ImageResult.strategy` and `.reason`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0011-extended-scene-imaging.md:38
msgid ""
"The image is an `ImageResult` (power per pixel and channel); "
"`to_wavecube()` gives a `Wavecube` of the same intensities for detectors "
"(its phase is meaningless, it is not to be propagated further)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0011-extended-scene-imaging.md:41
msgid "Alternatives considered"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0011-extended-scene-imaging.md:43
msgid ""
"A dedicated imaging element holding a reference to the downstream system:"
" it would break the purity of transfers (ADR-0002) and the acyclic graph."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0011-extended-scene-imaging.md:45
msgid ""
"Deciding the strategy from the element types (a coronagraph in the chain "
"→ decomposition): forbidden by principle 2 (no tests on class names); the"
" numerical probe works for any system, including user elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0011-extended-scene-imaging.md:47
msgid ""
"An analytic plate scale from the focal length: unknown for general "
"systems (relay optics, angular output grids); measuring it costs two "
"extra PSFs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0011-extended-scene-imaging.md:50
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0011-extended-scene-imaging.md:52
msgid ""
"Extended scenes behind coronagraphs and interferometers cost one mode per"
" non-dark scene pixel; scene grids must stay coarse enough (or use "
"`SceneToSources(threshold=...)`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0011-extended-scene-imaging.md:54
msgid ""
"The probe can be fooled by a system invariant at the probed point only; "
"users can force a strategy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0011-extended-scene-imaging.md:55
msgid ""
"Terrestrial scenes (P16) will reuse the frame mechanism; time-dependent "
"components already work through the clock of the context."
msgstr ""

